    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (87.14) serving as our clear focal point. His elite efficiency is driven by a prime matchup against Adams, capitalizing on favorable park factors and the stolen base upside that remains our primary strategic objective. **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **James Wood** (74.56) round out our top-tier outfield production; **James Wood** specifically benefits from an aggressive leadoff role and a robust 0.408 xwOBA, while **Mickey Moniak** projects to thrive against a vulnerable Kelly on the mound. **Gabriel Moreno** (71.10) also grades out as a high-floor start, elevated by his position in the three-hole and a soft matchup against Adams.\n\nIn terms of marginal decisions, **Travis Bazzana** (45.97) stands as the most notable exclusion from our active roster. While his platoon advantage is enticing, he ultimately failed to eclipse the efficiency scores of our starters in the middle infield, as the optimizer prioritized the established lineup spots of **Brice Turang** and **Isaac Paredes**. We are proceeding with caution regarding several wind-impacted matchups, specifically monitoring the \"Wind In\" advisory for **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Griffin Conine**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Austin Riley**. These conditions suppress home run potential, which\u2014when paired with the elite pitch-framing of opposing catchers or tough matchups against pitchers like Nola or Gausman\u2014necessitates a close watch on **Griffin Conine** and **Trevor Story**, who represent our lowest-scored active starts today.",
